rief) cites\n  a \"Strong Sell\" rating and the Seeking Alpha article on \"SoftBank Liquidation Threat\".\n  The ECGI working paper cited in the brief highlights governance entrenchment through\n  Shareholder Governance Agreement. These are data points, not verified filings.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments\n- \"ARM is a monopoly at 99% smartphone share\": killed because the *future* marginal dollar is\n  in data centers, where Arm is not dominant. If the data-center share story fails, the\n  remaining moat is a stable but slow-growing mobile royalty stream.\n- \"SBC is non-cash\": killed because net share issuance is positive, not offset by buybacks.\n  SBC is a real drain on per-share value for minority holders.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS (Layer 8)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nA. Methodology: PASS (blended engine; explicitly justified transition classification).\nB. Valuation: PASS with a caveat \u2014 the WACC of 12.8% may overstate risk for a wide-moat\n   franchise; sensitivity band shown (10% WACC \u2248 1.7x higher IV; 14% \u2248 0.6x lower).\nC. Bias: PASS \u2014 I report a bearish conclusion despite ARM's genuinely excellent franchise\n   quality; overconfidence check: the bull case is explicitly shown as plausible (20% weight).\nD. Consistency: PASS \u2014 the scenario assumptions use the same revenue/margin building blocks\n   as the DCF.\nE. Narrative: PASS \u2014 no platform premium without cash-flow reality; SBC-adjusted FCF is the\n   primary valuation denominator.\nF. Red Team: PASS \u2014 bear case presented from sa