on-like:** 52-week range $100.02\u2013$452.70; beta 3.909; 4.5x move in six months followed by \u221250% drawdown. This volatility profile is inconsistent with a Quality Compounder. [Actual \u2014 pack \u00a72, \u00a78]\n4. **Economic test fails Quality:** Adjusted ROIC \u224812.6% [Estimate] vs WACC 13%\u201322%. A Quality Compounder must earn >WACC; Arm does not.\n\n**Step 0-2. Engine Selection:** **Engine 4 \u2014 Expectation-Driven Valuation (Damodaran)** as primary. A **cross-check** using Engine 3's \"core anchor\" treatment is applied to the IP royalty base to avoid over-reliance on a single engine (Rule: no DCF-only conclusion).\n\n**Step 0-3. Transition Status \u2014 Pre-Transition:** Criteria for Option-Led \u2192 Product-Platform Hybrid:\n- Core Revenue >50%: **FAIL** (chip revenue = 0%)\n- GM >30%: **PASS** (first-gen AGI CPU GM \u224830% [Estimate \u2014 CFO Jason Child on Q4 FY26 call via TIKR])\n- FCF+ for 2 consecutive quarters: **FAIL** (adjusted FCF = \u2212$0.073B in FY2026)\n\u2192 **Pre-transition:** no blended engine required, but a 3.5x \"unexercised option\" frame is applied to chip revenue scenarios.\n\n**Step 0-4. Alternative-Engine Error Test:** Engine 1 (DCF on current earnings) would produce near-zero value due to SBC \u2265 FCF \u2014 transparent but incomplete (it ignores the option). Engine 3 (Hybrid) would overstate value by capitalizing an unshipped platform. Engine 2 (Cyclical) is inappropriate \u2014 Arm is not a commodity cycle business. Engine 4 correctly prices the probability-weighted claim on the AGI CPU.\n\n**Data/Tier declaration for this report:** Tiers 1\u20132 well covered [Filed/Actual]. Tiers 4\u20135 (future chip TAM, demand commitments, FTC outcome) dominate the valuation \u2014 **Model Confidence is formally downgraded to MEDIUM-LOW.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550