et) and demand backlog >$5B (vs $2B now).\n2. FTC investigation **closed without action** \u2014 removes the overhang.\n3. Data-center royalty growth accelerates >50% YoY, exceeding the IP-multiple expansion case.\n4. A **successful SoftBank secondary** that removes the overhang discount rather than flooding the market.\n5. Rate cuts: Fed eases before inflation is contained \u2192 multiple relief.\n\n### Downside Catalysts (support the SELL)\n1. FTC complaint filing or DOJ referral \u2192 royalty-rate compression.\n2. AGI CPU **delay** past Q4 FY27, or a Meta/OpenAI in-house silicon pivot.\n3. SBC/revenue stays >20% into FY2028 \u2192 GAAP EPS structurally capped near $1.30.\n4. Smartphone market contraction (already at 13-year low [Estimate \u2014 LinkedIn/LinkedIn News via web brief]) worsens.\n5. 10Y Treasury >5% \u2192 long-duration compression.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **Common bear trigger across a typical growth portfolio:** rising U.S. real rates, USD strength, and AI-capex digestion. ARM's beta of 3.909 aligns it with the *highest* beta bucket of those holdings.\n- **Tail correlation:** 2022-style rate shock \u2192 ARM would likely fall 40\u201360%, similar to NVDA/PLTR/TSLA. In a Stagflation regime (30% probability), ARM's long-duration cash flows are the most exposed asset class.\n- **Conditional VaR (CVaR) estimate [Assumption]:** 1-month 99% CVaR \u2248 25\u201335% (high beta + 12% short interest + binary headline risk). A 3-sigma event (FTC enforcement + chip delay) could gap the stock 30%+ in a single session.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n### Thesis Integrity Criteria (for future re-entry)\n| KPI | Threshold | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| AGI CPU production start | On track for Q4 FY27 | Company guidance [Actual] |\n| AGI CPU committed demand | >$5B by Q2 FY27 (vs $2B now) | Management disclosure |\n| Data-center royalty growth | >50% YoY quarterly | Segment data [need IR] |\n| **SBC / revenue** | **<15% by FY2028 and <10% by FY2030** | Quarterly filings |\n| GAAP EPS run-rate | >$2.00 by Q4 FY27 | Filings |\n| FTC investigation | Closed without enforcement | Press/regulatory |\n| Non-GAAP vs GAAP gap | Shrinking (SBC growth < revenue growth) | Filings |\n\n### Step 7-4. Pre-Mortem (if the SELL fails)\n*\"Three years from now, ARM trades at $500. Why?\"*\n1. **The AGI CPU was the 'next NVIDIA':** committed demand grew 10x to $30B+; hyperscalers (MSFT, AMZN, GOOG) all named as customers; production flawless. *Early warning: demand backlog >$5B at the next earnings call.*\n2. **AI-sovereignty procurement supercycle:** government-mandated domestic AI chip factories use Arm everywhere, and the FTC case is dropped for national-security reasons.\n3. **The market perma