1\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n2-1. Business in 3 sentences:\nArm designs and licenses the instruction-set architecture (ISA) and CPU microarchitecture used in effectively all smartphones (~99% share) and increasingly in data centers (Graviton, Grace, Axion-class CPUs), earning per-chip royalties plus upfront licensing fees. It is pivoting from pure IP licensing toward direct silicon (AGI CPU) with >$2B booked customer demand across FY27\u201328 (management assertion, Q1 FY27 call). It is the toll road of the computing world: zero fab cost, ~97% gross margin, and a 90%-controlled SoftBank parent.\nUnderstandability: High. This is one of the cleanest business models in technology.\n\n2-2. Moat Score (0\u20133 each):\n\u2022 Intangible assets (ISA, brand, patent estate): 3\n\u2022 Switching costs (software ecosystem, re-verify costs, decades of toolchains): 3\n\u2022 Network effects (ecosystem of 20M+ developers, 350B chips): 2\n\u2022 Cost advantage (asset-light, no fab): 3\n\u2022 Economies of scale (R&D spread over 30B+ chips/yr): 3\n\u2022 Regulatory barriers: 1\n\u2022 Data moat: 1\nTotal: 16/21 \u2192 FORTRESS moat.\nMoat direction: WIDENING in data center (share gains, cloud royalty momentum); STABLE in mobile (near-100% already). Evidence: data-center royalty revenue doubled in Q1 FY27 (management). [Actual \u2014 company assertion]\n\n2-3. Lynch Classification: FAST GROWER.\nKey checkpoint: verify growth durability. Revenue CAGR FY22-26: (4.920/2.703)^(1/4)\u22121 = 16.1%. [Arithmetic]\nGrowth accelerated to 23% in FY26 and ~22-24% guided for FY27. Sustainability: high for royalties (installed base compounding), but the market's implied decade of 30%+ growth is NOT sustainable without the silicon Hail Mary.\n\n2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard (all [Actual] unless noted):\n\u2022 Revenue growth: FY26 +23.0% YoY. [Actual]\n\u2022 Gross margin FY26: 97.5%. [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Operating margin FY26: 18.3%; 5-yr median 20.7%. [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 ROE FY26: 12.0% (NI 0.904 / avg equity 7.56). [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 GAAP diluted EPS FY26: $0.85. [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 FCF margin FY26: 19.9% (FCF 0.979 / rev 4.920, per pack's capex-exclsw definition). [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Net cash: \u2248 $2.67B (cash 2.751 + STI 0.850 + LTI 0.013 \u2212 total debt 0.457 \u2212 op-lease 0.432 \u2212 fin-lease 0.059). [Estimate \u2014 my aggregation, components [Actual]]\n\u2022 FCF quality: POOR \u2014 OCF swung $0.397B (FY25) to $1.524B (FY26), with \u0394WC consuming $1.295B in FY26 alone. FCF is lumpy and working-capital-driven. [Arithmetic]\nBalance-sheet judgment: Excellent (net cash, no leverage risk).\nEarnings-quality judgment: Concerning (SBC = 21% of revenue; WC swings dominate FCF; GAAP vs non-GAAP EPS gap is 2.1x).\n\n2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard:\n1. Buyback efficiency: 0/3 (net issuance +0.5% 1-yr; +1.0% 3-yr CAGR; no buyback). [Actual]\n2. M&A track record: 1/3 (limited history; no repeat impairment \u2014 but no evidence of value creation either).\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 (light asset base; incremental ROIC on the high-margin core >50% [Estimate]).\n4. Rationality of mix: 3/3 (R&D reinvestment in the core is rational; silicon enter \u2014 TBD [Assumption]).\n5. Guidance accuracy: 2/3 (FY26 revenue landed, but FCF trajectory missed badly and SBC surprises recur).\nInsider ownership bonus: CEO/insider = 0.07% (no signal); SoftBank ~87\u201390% control but with a $16B+$8B loan-raising arc that creates an OVERHANG, not alignment. \u22122 pts for the SoftBank loan. [Estimate \u2014 TradingKey/Economic Times via search]\nCapital Allocation total: 7/15 + insider adjustment \u22122 = 5/15 \u2192 MEDIOCRE.\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS (Layer 2.5)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n2.5-1. R&D Capitalization: R&D line NOT in pack. [Unconfirmed] Est. R&D \u2248 33% of revenue \u2248 $1.6B FY26. [Assumption \u2014 industry-model estimate] Capitalizing a 4-year vintage: unamortized asset \u2248 $3.5B; amortization \u2248 $1.3B. Adjusted EBIT = 0.900 + 1.6 \u2212 1.3 = $1.2B. [Estimate]\n2.5-2. SBC: Deducted as a cash expense throughout this report. FY26 SBC $1.052B = 21.4% of revenue. [Actual] SBC is the entire GAAP/non-GAAP gap (non-GAAP op margin \u224862% per TipRanks; GAAP 18.3% [Actual]).\n2.5-3. Operating leases: Capitalized into net debt (above): $0.432B. [Actual]\n2.5-4. Brand/Data assets: Not reliably estimable. [Unconfirmed \u2014 skipped]\n2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC: \u2248 10.7% (adjusted NOPAT ~$1.02B / adjusted IC ~$9.5B). [Estimate]\nGAAP ROIC \u2248 12.8%. [Estimate \u2014 15% tax assumption]\nAdjusted ROIC is LOWER than GAAP ROIC because the R&D asset adds capital. The vendor's 10.28% ROIC vs 24.25% WACC claim is directionally consistent with my estimate. This is a CRITICAL insight: on a capital-inclusive basis, Arm is not a >30% ROIC business; it is a ~11% ROIC business at a 137x earnings price.\n2.5-6. Owner earnings (FY26): NI 0.904 + D&A 0.249 \u2212 maintenance capex 0.150 [Assumption] \u2212 \u0394WC 1.295 = \u2212$0.292B. [Estimate]\nExcluding the suspicious \u0394WC swing: +$1.003B. [Estimate]\nThe 5-year \u0394WC series (+0.5, +1.2, +1.3) is a probable XBRL tag-change artifact (pack Section 0 warning). Both views were carried into scenarios.\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 BLENDED ENGINE (Engine 1 \u00d7 60% + Engine 4 \u00d7 40%) (Layers 0 & 3)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n0-1. Archetype: TRANSITIONING from Quality Compounder (B) toward Product-Platform Hybrid (D).\nTrigger evidence: (i) core royalty/license revenue still >85% of total [Estimate]; (ii) AGI CPU silicon launch with >$2B orders FY27-28 [Actual \u2014 mgmt]; (iii) capex rising from 2-4% to 11% of revenue (FY26) [Arithmetic]; (iv) FCF+ sustained. Criteria ~50-80% met \u2192 Blended Engine: Engine 1 DCF (60%) + Engine 4 Expectation Premium (40%). The Engine-4 premium is NOT added separately to the DCF \u2014 the DCF base already embeds moderate silicon; the 40% weight is expressed in the wide scenario distribution (Section 4). Alternative engine (pure DCF only) would understate optionality; alternative pure-Engine-4 would overstate base certainty.\n\n0-4. Why this archetype: (1) >90% of economics are still royalty/license annuity (2) Silicon is new and unproven GE at scale (3) The market is paying FOR the option, so the option must be explicitly tested, not buried.\n\n3-1. Discount rate derivation (WACC):\n\u2022 Risk-free: 4.74% (10Y UST, 2026-08-21) [Actual]\n\u2022 ERP: 4.5% [Assumption \u2014 standard long-horizon US ERP]\n\u2022 Beta: 1.35 [Assumption \u2014 vendor beta 3.909 rejected: unstated window/benchmark, post-IPO noise. Semiconductor IP peer betas ~1.2\u20131.5. Using 1.35 is generous given the vendor's own value.]\n\u2022 Cost of equity = 4.74% + 1.35(4.5%) = 10.8% \u2192 11.0% [Estimate]\n\u2022 Net cash position \u2192 WACC = Cost of Equity \u2248 11.0% [Estimate]\n\u2022 Cross-check: vendor WACC 24.25% is the same rejection; my 11% is APPROXIMATE ONLY and is the single most important assumption in this report.\n\n3-2. Explicit forecast \u2014 BASE CASE (all $B unless noted):\n\n[Assumption \u2014 every line sourced below]\nRevenue path: FY27 $6.10B (Q1 actual $1.29B + Q2 guide $1.38B + H2 ramp \u21d2 +24%;\n                          cross-checked against FY26 $4.92B + 23% guide) [Actual Q1/Q2; path [Estimate]]\n                          FY28 $7.60B (+24.6%; AGI CPU $2B orders convert partially) [Estimate]\n                          FY29 $9.40B (+23.7%) | FY30 $11.30B (+20.2%) | FY31 $13.40B (+18.6%)\n                          Implied CAGR FY26-31: 22.2% \u2014 BELOW consensus ($+35.5% forward row, horizon undefined) [Estimate]\nGross margin: FY27 92% \u2192 FY28 88% \u2192 FY29 85% \u2192 FY30 83% \u2192 FY31 82%\n                          (silicon mix drag from 97.5% today) [Assumption]\nGAAP operating margin: FY27 22% \u2192 FY28 24% \u2192 FY29 25% \u2192 FY30 26% \u2192 FY31 27%\n                          (FY26 = 18.3% [Arithmetic]; SBC stays ~18-21% of revenue) [Assumption]\nTax rate: 15% (IP-heavy global minimum structure) [Assumption \u2014 pack tax inputs provably broken]\nCapex: 10% of revenue (FY26 was 11% incl. capitalized-software risk) [Assumption]\nD&A: 5% of revenue (FY26 = 5.1%) [Assumption/Arithmetic]\n\u0394WC: 15% of \u0394Revenue (normalized; pack trend is a probable artifact but I keep conservatism) [Assumption]\n\n| FY | Revenue | GM% | OpM% | EBIT | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | FCF |\n| FY27| 6.10 | 92% | 22% | 1.34 | 1.14 | 0.31 | 0.61 | 0.18 | 0.66 |\n| FY28| 7.60 | 88% | 24% | 1.82 | 1.55 | 0.38 | 0.76 | 0.23 | 0.95 |\n| FY29| 9.40 | 85% | 25% | 2.35 | 2.00 | 0.47 | 0.94 | 0.27 | 1.26 |\n| FY30|11.30 | 83% | 26% | 2.94 | 2.50 | 0.57 | 1.13 | 0.29 | 1.65 |\n| FY31|13.40 | 82% | 27% | 3.62 | 3.08 | 0.67 | 1.34 | 0.32 | 2.09 |\n\n3-3. Terminal value (growth-contributive method):\ng = 3.5% (\u2264 nominal GDP) [Assumption]; terminal ROIC = 25% [Assumption]\nTerminal FCF31 = NOPAT31 \u00d7 (1 \u2212 g/ROIC) = 3.08 \u00d7 0.86 = 2.65\nTV = 2.65 \u00d7 1.035 / (0.11 \u2212 0.035) = $36.6B [Arithmetic]\n\n3-4. Intrinsic value \u2014 BASE:\nPV(FCF27\u201331) @11% = 0.59 + 0.77 + 0.92 + 1.09 + 1.24 = $4.61B\nPV(TV) = 36.6 \u00d7 0.5935 = $21.73B\nEV = $26.34B\nNet cash: +$2.67B (components stated in 2-4) [Estimate]\nEquity value = $29.0B\nDiluted shares (1.068B now + 1%/yr dilution \u2248 1.09B avg) [Assumption]\nBASE IV = $29.0B / 1.09B = $26.6/share \u2248 $26 [Estimate]\n\n3-5. Tornado sensitivity (\u00b11\u03c3 \u2014 top 3 variables):\n1. WACC: 8% \u2192 IV $45; 11% \u2192 $26; 14% \u2192 $16 [Arithmetic]\n2. FY27-31 revenue CAGR: +5pp \u2192 IV ~$38; \u22125pp \u2192 IV ~$17 [Estimate]\n3. SBC/capital intensity: SBC held flat (improvement) \u2192 IV ~$33; SBC grows 20%/yr \u2192 IV ~$21 [Estimate]\nConclusion: NO reasonable single-variable move approaches the market price of $243. Even the 8%-WACC-and-bull-revenue combination stays below ~$60.\n\n3-6. Reverse DCF \u2014 what the market prices:\nTo justify $243 at 11% discount over 5 years and a 30x exit multiple on non-GAAP EPS:\nRequired FY31 non-GAAP EPS = $243 \u00d7 (1.11^5) / 30 = $13.65\nAt a generous 40x exit: required FY31 EPS = $10.24\nArm management's own FY2031 target: >$9 non-GAAP EPS [Actual \u2014 investor day via Investing.com headline]\n=> The current price implies management BEATS its own 2031 target by 14\u201352%, with zero discount for the probability of failure. Verdict: expectations are EXCESSIVE.\n\n3-7. Cross-check \u2014 single-line multiples:\nTrailing GAAP P/E: 277x [vendor]; Non-GAAP 137x. [Arithmetic: 243.32/1.77]\nNeither multiple leaves room for error. Even a 30% de-rating to 96x non-GAAP still prices in perfection. Consensus forward PEG 2.2 is misleading (short-horizon growth).\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS (Layer 3.5)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n3.5-1. Competitive response: If AGI CPU succeeds, AMD/Intel/Qualcomm and hyperscaler in-house teams (Google, Amazon, Microsoft) will accelerate custom Arm/X86/RISC-V silicon; the licensing model is structurally protected, but direct-silicon unit economics could see margin erosion. Counter-move impact: \u22121. [Assumption]\n3.5-2. Reflexivity: HIGH. Rising price \u2192 SBC attracts talent, SoftBank uses Arm shares as loan collateral (positive loop); falling price \u2192 SoftBank liquidity pressure, \"Strong Sell\" narratives, margin-call overhang (negative loop). The stock fell 28% in a month after AGI CPU hype \u2014 the loop is already demonstrated. [Estimate]\n3.5-3. Customer evolution: Data-center customers are 5-10 hyperscalers with enormous negotiation power vs Arm's mobile base of hundreds of diversified licensees. As penetration grows, royalty per-chip compresses (Nvidia/Amazon in-house design). LTV/CAC not disclosed [Unconfirmed]. Assume royalty-per-device declines 2-4%/yr after FY30. [Assumption]\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (Bayesian \u2014 Layer 4)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nPrior: Layer 1.5 base rates (platform transition 20-30% success). Likelihood updates: Q1 FY27 revenue beat (+22% y/y), AGI CPU $2B orders, FY26 non-GAAP EPS $1.77 \u2014 these support the \"business is executing\" hypothesis; but the price already moved from $452 to $243 BEFORE these confirmations \u2014 meaning the soft data was already in the price. Posterior weights reflect this: the business succeeds, but the investment lags.\n\n\u2022 BEAR (35%): Revenue FY31 $9.0B (CAGR ~13%), GAAP OpM 20%; GAAP EPS FY31 ~$1.4; SoftBank liquidity overhang persists; Qualcomm Nuvia trial (Q4 CY26) unsettles royalty model; RISC-V share gains in IoT.\n  IV \u2248 $15/share [Estimate]\n\u2022 BASE (45%): The forecast in Section 3. IV \u2248 $26/share [Estimate]\n\u